<Item XName="Note1" UserName="Note1" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>1</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;DIV style=&quot;BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 1pt solid; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; PADDING-TOP: 0in; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in; mso-element: para-border-div; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .75pt&quot;&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; BORDER-BOTTOM: medium none; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0in; TEXT-ALIGN: center; PADDING-TOP: 0in; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .75pt; mso-padding-alt: 0in 0in 1.0pt 0in&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 18pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;Adaptive Beamforming Example&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = &quot;o&quot; ns = &quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&apos;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue Example Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;************************************************&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;Simulation Task&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;************************************************&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;This example demos how to use RADAR_ADBF model to estimate the weights with received signal samples across all receiving channels (with &quot;guessed&quot; incoming signal directions), and the weights are fed into RADAR_DBF to implement digital beamforming, realizing adaptive beamforming for jamming suppression purposes. &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;************************************************&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;Workspace Description&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;************************************************&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;In this example, we designed two incoming signals from different directions: one interested signal from theta = 30 deg, while the other jammer signal is from theta = 60 deg. Both signal directions are designed by Phased Array Antenna Rx models (RADAR_PhasedArrayRx). &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;The combined signal is imported into RADAR_ADBF which is applied to generate the adaptive estimated weights for all receiver channels. The adaptive Rx weights are divided into two paths: &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;1) For the upper path, we designed a theta sweep mathlang block which displays the ADBF results in theta-pattern format; &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;2) For the lower path, we need to realign the weights for RADAR_DBF model. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;Firstly, we use the commutator block to align the signal on a Rx channel group basis. That is, for instance, we have 16 channels, then the complex beam weights are aligned by the weights of the first 16-Rx group, and then a second 16-Rx group, and so on. In the corresponding sink data limit, we set to 10 such groups.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;Then, we use the PRI data length (NumSamp_PRI) to upsample (repeating) the regrouped weights to fit the length of PRI. After that, we apply the distributor to rescale the output weights on a PRI-by-PRI basis, to fit the input data length requirement of RADAR_DBF block.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;With the adaptive beamforming design described above, the desired steering direction can be set to near to the real interested direction. In this example we propose 35 deg, and both the ADBF theta-sweep pattern and the DBF output signal have shown imperfect suppression of jamming signal. (If the user tries setting the ADBF desired theta direction to = 30 deg, then the jammer would be perfectly suppressed.)&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;NOTE: &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;I&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;Desired Beamforming Direction Setting&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/I&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;The angle of interested direction can be set with parameter Theta (elevation angle in antenna frame) and Phi (azimuth angle in antenna frame) when input ports el and az are not connected. When they are connected, the angle values in the parameter are disabled and the angles are decided by the input angle values.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;</Text>
